  "ingredients": [
    "8 ounce strawberries",
    "1/4 cup erythritol (powdered)",
    "2 tablespoon chia seeds",
    "1/4 cup water"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Measure out the strawberries and slice into small cubes. The bigger the cubes, the bigger the remaining pieces in the jam will be.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/strawberry-chia-seed-jam/#wprm-recipe-51209-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7744.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the erythritol to a spice grinder and grind until powdered. Take care when removing the lid! By letting the powder settle first, you will eliminate an unwanted cloud of sweetener.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/strawberry-chia-seed-jam/#wprm-recipe-51209-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7748.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place the cubed strawberries into a pan over medium heat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/strawberry-chia-seed-jam/#wprm-recipe-51209-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7752.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the powdered erythritol and mix well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/strawberry-chia-seed-jam/#wprm-recipe-51209-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7760.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Let sit over the heat for a while. The strawberries will naturally release water and juice as they heat up.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/strawberry-chia-seed-jam/#wprm-recipe-51209-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7770.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mash the strawberries using a potato masher (or fork) and allow the mixture to come to a boil.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/strawberry-chia-seed-jam/#wprm-recipe-51209-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7774.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boil for about 5–8 minutes, until thickened slightly.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/strawberry-chia-seed-jam/#wprm-recipe-51209-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7777.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Measure out the chia seeds.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/strawberry-chia-seed-jam/#wprm-recipe-51209-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7765.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the chia seeds and water to the jam and stir for 1–2 minutes. Remove from the heat and let cool for about 15 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/strawberry-chia-seed-jam/#wprm-recipe-51209-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7783.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Transfer to a mason jar and serve or save for later. Enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/strawberry-chia-seed-jam/#wprm-recipe-51209-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7787.jpg"
    }
  ],
